---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../../components/_breadcrumbs';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';

const crumbs = breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Symptoms', href: '/pms/' }, { name: 'Crying', href: '/pms/crying/' }]);
---

<Page
  title="Crying before your period: why, and what to do · Niyora"
  description="Crying before your period, sometimes over nothing, is common and real. Here is the science behind premenstrual tearfulness, and what helps in the moment."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/pms/crying/"
  jsonLd={crumbs}
>
  <section class="s hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Crying before your period</div>
    <h1>Crying before your period: why, and what to do</h1>
    <p class="lead">In the days before your period, tears can come easily, sometimes over something small, sometimes over nothing you can point to. This is not you being fragile. It is a normal hormonal shift landing on a sensitive nervous system, and it lifts as the shift passes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Why you feel heavy and tearful</h2>
    <div class="science">
      <p>Before your period, the part of you that reaches for joy is turned down, like someone lowered the dial. So forcing yourself to feel happy is like flooring a car in neutral. The engine is fine. It just needs the dial turned back up, and that happens on its own.</p>
      <p>Your hormone levels are normal. Women who feel this heaviness and women who feel steady have the same measured levels. The difference is how strongly your nervous system responds to the ordinary rise and fall, and some systems feel it more. The tears are a real response to a real shift, not a sign something is wrong with you.</p>
      <p>And it passes. When your hormones move on, usually once your period starts, the heaviness lifts. That relief you feel afterward is your body coming back online. It rolls in, and it rolls out, every cycle.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>What helps in the moment</h2>
    <p class="lead">Niyora is built for the moment the wave hits. Three small steps, about a minute, then you close it.</p>
    <div class="rrr-grid">
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Reflect</div>
        <p>Name the moment. Seeing that the heaviness is the dial turned low for a few days, not the truth about your life, lets you stop arguing with the feeling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Regulate</div>
        <p>Settle your body in about a minute. A slower breath, warmth, a steady presence. You cannot always think your way calm, so let the body lead and the mind follows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Respond</div>
        <p>With your body a little steadier, you can let the tears pass without spiralling into what they must mean, and move through the day with a clearer head.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Keep reading</h2>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/blog/how-to-stop-crying/" class="btn ghost">How to stop crying when it won't stop</a>
      <a href="/blog/common-emotions-during-pms/" class="btn ghost">The common emotions during PMS</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Not sure the tearful week is PMS?</h2>
    <p class="lead">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/quiz" class="btn">Take the quiz</a>
      <a href={downloads.appStore} class="btn ghost">Get Niyora</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Page-specific only: the science block and the R/R/R grid. Shared chrome
     (sheet, sections, dividers, type scale, buttons, footer) comes from Page. */
  .science {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.28);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .science p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .science p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .rrr-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .rrr-card {
    padding: 24px 22px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .rrr-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.9);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .rrr-card p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82); }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .s { padding: 56px 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    .rrr-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .science p { font-size: 16px; }
  }
</style>
